# Pipeline cache
scripts/pipeline/.cache/
scripts/pipeline/cache/
scoring-output/

# Phase 1.5 ingestion — large source files (P15-A-3 + P15-B-2, 8 June 2026)
# These exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit on push. Operator downloads
# locally; the bbox-clipped per-country CSVs that derive from them ARE
# committed (small, ~10-25 MB total).
#
# Sources:
#   gshm-2023-1.tif        — GEM 2023.1 Global Seismic Hazard Map (~173 MB)
#                            Download: https://cloud.openquake.org/s/6SnFk2f92JEr76H
#                            License: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
#   era5land_*.nc          — ERA5-Land NetCDF intermediate cache (~50-200 MB each)
#                            Re-downloadable via CDS API; not deliverable artifacts
scripts/pipeline/data/cross-cutting/gshm-2023-1.tif
scripts/pipeline/data/cross-cutting/*.tif
*.nc
*.grib
*.grib2

# Phase 1 housekeeping (8 June 2026): backup files are local-only working state
*.pre-*-backup
*.pre-*.backup
*.bak
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Discipline #36 cross-border audit (18 June 2026): per-country rejection
# logs from scripts/remediate_cross_border.py + clean_grid_geo.py. These
# are forensic audit-trail artifacts (full record of which substations
# were removed at remediation time) — useful locally for review but too
# large for the repo (Canada's alone is 52 MB). The audit memo
# CROSS_BORDER_SUBSTATION_AUDIT_20260618.md preserves the per-country
# summary; the full rejection lists stay on the operator's machine.
*/ingestion_rejected_*.json

# OneDrive / FUSE synced-cloud filesystem artifacts (Mac client leaves .fuse_hidden*
# during file operations while the sync daemon holds handles open)
.fuse_hidden*

# v4.23 workstream L1 connector ingestion caches (13 July 2026) — these are
# operator-runtime downloads from federal canonical sources + OSM Overpass.
# Contents:
#   canada/_canvec_cache/       NRCan CanVec 50K Res_MGT GDB + PDF (37 MB)
#   norway/_nve_cache/          NVE Nettanlegg WFS response cache (209 MB)
#   mexico/_osm_cache/          OSM Overpass query response cache (~1 MB)
#   austria/_osm_cache/         OSM Overpass query response cache (empty during sandbox block)
#   greenland/_osm_cache/       OSM Overpass query response cache (small)
# All are re-fetchable on demand via each L1 connector.  Downstream federation +
# merge outputs (canada/ssi-data.json, norway/ssi-data.json, etc.) ARE committed.
scripts/pipeline/data/*/_canvec_cache/
scripts/pipeline/data/*/_nve_cache/
scripts/pipeline/data/*/_osm_cache/

# v4.23 workstream intermediate federation JSONs — these are the raw L1 output
# before merge into per-country ssi-data.json.  Regenerable on demand.
scripts/pipeline/data/*/substations_federated.json
scripts/pipeline/data/*/transmission_lines_federated.json

# Pipeline run artifacts (13 July 2026)
pipeline-run.log
pipeline-report-*.json

# Wave 2 v4.23 — Overpass raw fetch cache (per-country _osm_cache subdirs;
# regenerable via python -m scripts.pipeline.ingestion.<country>.osm_overpass;
# NOT source of truth; content-hashed by cache_path_for(query) per Convention #78)
scripts/pipeline/ingestion/data/
scripts/pipeline/data/*/_osm_cache/

# Wave 4 v4.23 per-country OSM Overpass raw cache dirs (Sweden P32 +
# Portugal P33 + Italy P34 + Japan P35 + Spain P36 + France P37 + Germany
# P38 + US P39 pattern). Files are regenerable via:
#   python -m scripts.pipeline.ingestion.<country>.osm_overpass
# NEVER committed — sibling countries already have _cache/ untracked;
# France P37 got caught by `git add -A france/` and hit GitHub 100 MB
# hard limit on overpass-lines-raw.json (216 MB).
*/_cache/

# Wave 4 v4.23 per-country ingestion log files. Local audit-trail
# artifacts only. Sibling countries have these untracked already.
*/v4_23-osm-overpass.log
*/v4_23-merge.log
*/v4_23-phase-4c-refresh.log

# Task #452 Step 4 (23 Jul 2026): Niva 2023 gridded net-migration raster —
# ~10.5 MB GeoTIFF from Nature Human Behaviour paper (Zenodo 7997134,
# CC BY 4.0). Regenerable via:
#   curl -L -o docs/audits/raster_netMgr_2000_2019_20yrSum.tif \
#     "https://zenodo.org/records/7997134/files/raster_netMgr_2000_2019_20yrSum.tif?download=1"
# Ref: Niva et al. 2023, Nature Human Behaviour 7:2023-2037,
# DOI 10.1038/s41562-023-01689-4. NEVER committed — Convention #79 sharding
# doesn't apply to source rasters; keep local-only.
docs/audits/raster_netMgr_*.tif

# Task #451 Step 4 (23 Jul 2026): GHSL Population Grid raster —
# ~500 MB extracted GeoTIFF from EC JRC / Copernicus. Regenerable via:
#   curl -L -o /tmp/ghs_pop.zip https://jeodpp.jrc.ec.europa.eu/ftp/jrc-opendata/GHSL/GHS_POP_GLOBE_R2023A/GHS_POP_E2025_GLOBE_R2023A_54009_1000/V1-0/GHS_POP_E2025_GLOBE_R2023A_54009_1000_V1_0.zip
#   unzip -j /tmp/ghs_pop.zip 'GHS_POP_E2025_GLOBE_R2023A_54009_1000_V1_0.tif' -d docs/audits/
# License: EC JRC / Copernicus Emergency Management Service — attribution-required
# open license (Convention #7 + #60 compatible). NEVER committed — exceeds
# GitHub 100 MB hard limit.
docs/audits/GHS_POP_*.tif
docs/audits/GHS_POP_*.zip
docs/audits/ghs_pop.*
*.bak_shardfix
*.log
logs/
scripts/pipeline/ingestion/*/cache/

# dedupe audit sidecars live in the SSI Index folder, not the repo
ssi_dedupe_audit_*.json

# Count-refresh backups (refresh_country_counts.py --from-data) and the
# quarantine folder used instead of deletion, since device tooling cannot rm.
*.pre-count-refresh-*.backup
_to_delete/
